WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.710
- Canada is a really attractive place

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:07.960
to pursue AI because it's a
very supportive environment.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.530
And we're also, as researchers,

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.680
very supportive of each other.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.050
- [Samira] We have some of
the biggest labs in the field

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.630
and that in general
makes it so easy to start

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:17.904
and grow in this field.

00:00:17.904 --> 00:00:19.120
- [Sarath] The entire
deep learning revolution

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.540
actually happened in Canada
and we were able to do this

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.908
because there was a constant
support from the government

00:00:23.908 --> 00:00:25.120
and CIFAR.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.060
- [Martha] The great thing about the CIFAR

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.580
Pan-Canadian AI Strategy

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.000
is that it's focused on AI expertise.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.020
The funding model in Canada
largely focuses on funding

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.920
people rather than projects.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.480
And this means that you're
free to pursue the research

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.050
that you think is important.

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:42.250
- [Samira] I like how the
AI community is connected

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.000
and works together and
push the boundary of AI.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:45.900
- [Graham] Well, it's really

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.600
a highly collaborative environment

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.160
that supports joint projects
and provides resources

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.003
to researchers across the country.

